WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.227 --> 00:00:18.760
Jonathan and his parents got to the field early on Saturday afternoon for the game.

2
00:00:18.761 --> 00:00:24.926
His dad set up their chairs near Carlos' mom and some other parents.

3
00:00:24.927 --> 00:00:31.155
Jonathan spotted Marissa on the sideline. She wore a cute yellow sundress and a turquoise straw hat.

4
00:00:31.156 --> 00:00:34.734
Marissa glanced at Jonathan, frowned, and turned away.

5
00:00:34.735 --> 00:00:39.852
Jonathan took a deep breath and walked over to her.

6
00:00:39.853 --> 00:00:42.814
Marissa scowled. "What do you want?"

7
00:00:42.814 --> 00:00:46.939
Jonathan took a very deep breath. "I want to apologize.

8
00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:52.720
I mean, I don't want to apologize, because it's really difficult for me because I'm so nervous.

9
00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:58.211
But also, I do want to apologize because you deserve it. An apology, I mean."

10
00:00:58.212 --> 00:01:03.891
Marissa raised her eyebrows at him as he babbled on. At least she'd stopped scowling.

11
00:01:03.892 --> 00:01:09.209
"I shouldn't have mad-mouthed your family. I mean, bad-mouthed your family," Jonathan said.

12
00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:16.958
"I didn't know that was your family. But now I know. I mean, I realized it right after I said it. I mean . . ."

13
00:01:16.959 --> 00:01:22.482
Jonathan took another deep breath. "I'm really sorry."

14
00:01:22.483 --> 00:01:25.049
Marissa looked slightly amused.

15
00:01:25.049 --> 00:01:28.452
"That was the longest, most confusing apology I've ever heard."

16
00:01:28.453 --> 00:01:29.937
"I'm sorry for that."

17
00:01:29.938 --> 00:01:34.034
"Now you're apologizing for your apology?" Marissa smiled.

18
00:01:34.034 --> 00:01:39.540
"It's okay, Jonathan. I understand what you were trying to say. And I forgive you."

19
00:01:39.541 --> 00:01:46.445
Jonathan took another deep breath. This one was a big sigh of relief.

20
00:01:46.446 --> 00:01:53.528
"I mean, I didn't like hearing you insult my brother and father," Marissa went on. "But I understand why people get frustrated with them.

21
00:01:53.529 --> 00:01:58.360
Dad gets carried away by Max's soccer skills, and he forgets about the rest of the team.

22
00:01:58.361 --> 00:02:01.064
And Max just goes along with Dad."

23
00:02:01.065 --> 00:02:05.264
Jonathan nodded. Then he tried to think of something nice to say.

24
00:02:05.264 --> 00:02:10.009
"Max is really talented, and your father seems to know a lot about soccer."

25
00:02:10.010 --> 00:02:14.747
"True," she said. "But Dad needs to learn how to chill out."

26
00:02:14.748 --> 00:02:18.561
"Team meeting!" Coach Wattenbarger yelled just then.

27
00:02:18.562 --> 00:02:20.812
"Boys, get over here! Now!"

28
00:02:20.813 --> 00:02:23.485
"I have to go," Jonathan said.

29
00:02:23.485 --> 00:02:26.313
"Let's talk again soon," Marissa said.

30
00:02:26.314 --> 00:02:32.481
"Okay!" Jonathan wanted to act cool, but a huge grin took over his whole face.

31
00:02:32.481 --> 00:02:36.985
He got to the meeting just as his coach started talking.

32
00:02:36.986 --> 00:02:40.474
"We're playing the Spitting Cobras today," the coach said.

33
00:02:40.475 --> 00:02:46.568
"They won their first two games. But we can beat them if everyone keeps passing the ball to Max."

34
00:02:46.569 --> 00:02:49.569
Jonathan started to protest. "Coach—"

35
00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:55.705
"Dad. I'm too sick to play today," Max said. He clutched his stomach.

36
00:02:55.705 --> 00:03:01.036
The coach frowned. "You told me your stomach hurt, but you didn't want to go to the doctor."

37
00:03:01.037 --> 00:03:04.869
"My stomach doesn't hurt enough for a doctor visit," Max said.

38
00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:08.638
"Then it doesn't hurt enough to skip the game," the coach snapped.

39
00:03:08.639 --> 00:03:11.155
"You'll get in there and play, like a pro!"

40
00:03:11.156 --> 00:03:14.478
"Poor Max," Jonathan thought.

41
00:03:14.478 --> 00:03:16.876
"I also think I'm coming down with a bad cold."

42
00:03:16.877 --> 00:03:26.119
Max sneezed loudly, and Carlos caught Jonathan's eye as if they were both thinking the same thing—was that a fake sneeze?

43
00:03:26.119 --> 00:03:33.617
"Max, we can't win without you," Coach Wattenbarger was saying. "You're the backbone of this team!"

44
00:03:33.618 --> 00:03:37.448
"No, I'm not," Max replied in a shaky voice.

45
00:03:37.449 --> 00:03:43.277
"And you can win without me. Jonathan is really good. He can play forward today."

46
00:03:43.278 --> 00:03:47.497
Jonathan shook his head. "I'm not nearly as good as you, Max."

47
00:03:47.498 --> 00:03:53.011
"Max, you're the best player in the league," his father said for the millionth time that season.

48
00:03:53.012 --> 00:03:58.755
"I'm the sickest player in the league today." Max bent over and coughed.

49
00:03:58.756 --> 00:04:06.756
Coach Wattenbarger sighed. "All right, Max. Rest on the sideline. Jonathan, play forward."

50
00:04:06.757 --> 00:04:14.167
Jonathan had been dying to play forward since the soccer season had started. But he didn't want to do it now, not without Max.

51
00:04:14.168 --> 00:04:24.153
He hurried toward Max and took him aside. "You may be the best soccer player in the league, but you're the worst actor in the world," he whispered.

52
00:04:24.154 --> 00:04:32.306
"Stop pretending to be sick. Our team needs you. And we want you to play—as long as the rest of us can play with you!"

53
00:04:32.307 --> 00:04:33.971
Max shook his head.

54
00:04:33.972 --> 00:04:36.717
"Come on, Max," Jonathan said.

55
00:04:36.717 --> 00:04:42.213
"Everyone get on the field. The game's about to start!" Coach Wattenbarger yelled.

56
00:04:42.214 --> 00:04:46.632
Max didn't move. "Just go, Jonathan!"

57
00:04:46.633 --> 00:04:50.977
Jonathan glared at him before running onto the field.

58
00:04:50.978 --> 00:04:54.378
He and his teammates lined up against the Spitting Cobras.

59
00:04:54.378 --> 00:04:57.323
He hoped the Spitting Cobras didn't actually spit!

60
00:04:57.324 --> 00:05:01.196
The Cobras had two substitutes and were big and fierce-looking.

61
00:05:01.196 --> 00:05:05.859
Meanwhile, because of Max's "illness," the Wattenbargers were missing a player.

62
00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:10.783
Facing the Cobras, the Wattenbargers appeared small and timid to Jonathan.

63
00:05:10.784 --> 00:05:20.837
The Spitting Cobras started strong. They passed the ball up the field, near the goal. One of their forwards took a shot.

64
00:05:20.838 --> 00:05:27.829
Luckily, a Wattenbarger defender blocked the ball, kicking it to a Wattenbarger midfielder, who kicked it to Jonathan.

65
00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:34.756
Here, finally, was Jonathan's chance to score!

66
00:05:34.757 --> 00:05:43.336
But a huge Spitting Cobra moved in front of him. Jonathan looked around but couldn't find anyone open for a pass.

67
00:05:43.337 --> 00:05:53.989
He didn't like the pressure of being the only forward. He tried to dribble the ball, but the huge Cobra in front of him forced him out of bounds.

68
00:05:53.990 --> 00:06:03.809
The huge Cobra took the throw-in. He threw the ball far up the field to his teammate, who kicked it to another teammate.

69
00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:10.547
That guy kicked it just out of reach of the Wattenbarger goalie and into the goal.

70
00:06:10.548 --> 00:06:17.228
Jonathan looked at Max in dismay. But on the sideline, Max just stared down at the ground.

71
00:06:17.229 --> 00:06:22.718
The Spitting Cobras didn't score any more goals in the first half, but neither did the Wattenbargers.

72
00:06:22.719 --> 00:06:28.709
Jonathan was grateful that he got to play his hardest instead of just giving Max the ball as he'd done the first two games.

73
00:06:28.710 --> 00:06:34.532
But it didn't feel right for Max to be on the sideline. Plus, he wouldn't mind scoring a goal.

74
00:06:34.533 --> 00:06:39.916
Once the Wattenbargers got off the field, their coach shouted, "What a terrible first half!

75
00:06:39.917 --> 00:06:44.373
Take a two-minute water break. Then get over here for a team meeting."

76
00:06:44.373 --> 00:06:50.224
Jonathan grabbed his water bottle and hurried to where Max was sitting.

77
00:06:50.224 --> 00:06:52.529
"We need you on the field."

78
00:06:52.530 --> 00:06:56.418
Max rubbed his stomach. "I'm sick."

79
00:06:56.419 --> 00:07:01.699
"I think you're just sick of your dad's coaching style and too scared to tell him," Jonathan said.

80
00:07:01.700 --> 00:07:07.834
"Just like I was scared to apologize to you and your sister. But after I did, I felt a lot better."

81
00:07:07.835 --> 00:07:10.155
Max sighed.

82
00:07:10.156 --> 00:07:14.233
"Besides, you can't pretend to be sick all season.

83
00:07:14.233 --> 00:07:17.820
We still have a bunch of games left," Jonathan said.

84
00:07:17.821 --> 00:07:30.233
Max sighed again. "Okay, I'll talk to my dad. But he won't like what I have to say."
